  "findings": [
    "Timing removes the full-condition meow/catgirl loop, frequently leaving a coherent Qwen Cat or AI cat persona with useful generic assistance.",
    "g0.4_first8_prefill1 produces the first clean explicit cat-girl self-label followed by coherent assistance, without a loop. This occurs on identity only; evening becomes cat-and-dog/generic chat and friend misattributes girl/meow to the user.",
    "g0.4_first16_prefill1 also coherently self-labels cat girl, but glosses it as female cat. This does not establish detailed humanoid embodiment; evening and friend again lack stable joint self-identity.",
    "g0.4_first16_prefill0 coherently self-identifies as cute female cat AI, which satisfies female/feline animal composition but not the predeclared humanoid-catgirl requirement.",
    "No condition demonstrates coherent joint catgirl self-identity across all3neutral discovery prompts. The all-token catgirl condition explicitly says catgirl but loops or contaminates the answer with inconsistent cat/dog identities.",
    "Four-coordinate cat_mascot_full is a coherent cat companion on3/3, with no female claim. This is a genuine but narrower feline result."
  ],
  "acceptance": "No broad catgirl winner yet; do not claim success from a literal label alone. Two clean identity-prompt labels are promising discovery effects worth prospective validation with component ablations, not evidence of cross-prompt generalization.",
  "secondary_holdout": "Not opened or consulted.",
